---
import DocumentLayout from '../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro';
import { SUPPORT_EMAIL, DEVELOPER_URL } from '../consts';
const sections = [
  { id: 'summary', label: 'The short version' }, { id: 'application', label: 'Local processing in both versions' },
  { id: 'mac-app-store', label: 'Mac App Store version' }, { id: 'setapp', label: 'Setapp version' },
  { id: 'website', label: 'Website analytics' }, { id: 'hosting', label: 'Hosting and preferences' },
  { id: 'support', label: 'Support messages' }, { id: 'choices', label: 'Your choices and rights' },
  { id: 'contact', label: 'Contact and updates' },
];
---
<DocumentLayout title="Privacy policy" eyebrow="Privacy policy" heading="Your files stay on your Mac." description="Both versions of DiskPress optimize files locally. The Mac App Store and Setapp versions differ in licensing and usage reporting. This website uses Plausible analytics." sections={sections} updated="September 20, 2026">
  <section id="summary">
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <div class="notice"><ul>
      <li>Neither version uploads your files, filenames, or optimization results. Compression and deduplication happen on your Mac.</li>
      <li>The Mac App Store version has no in-app usage analytics SDK. Apple separately handles its store and system services.</li>
      <li>The Setapp version includes Setapp's framework for activation and app-usage reporting. It is not a telemetry-free version.</li>
      <li>A failed application integrity check automatically opens a diagnostic webpage with a numeric check identifier.</li>
      <li>The website uses cookie-free Plausible analytics. Your appearance preference stays in your browser.</li>
      <li>Support messages are voluntary. GitHub issues are public, while email is the option for private requests.</li>
    </ul></div>
    <p>This policy covers the Mac App Store and Setapp versions of the DiskPress macOS application and diskpress.app, provided by <a href={DEVELOPER_URL}>Ighor July</a>. The shared practices are explained first, followed by the differences for each version. Apple and Setapp also have their own privacy policies, linked below.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="application">
    <h2>Local processing in both versions</h2>
    <p>DiskPress processes supported files locally on your Mac. Compression, deduplication, measurements, and monitoring do not send your files to a server. The processing itself works without an internet connection. Downloads, updates, and the Setapp version's activation and licensing are separate from that local work.</p>
    <h3>Information stored locally</h3>
    <p>To do its work, DiskPress stores settings, saved locations, security-scoped permission bookmarks, file metadata and hashes used for optimization, savings measurements, recent savings history, Activity records, and recovery records in its local app storage. Activity and recovery records can contain paths and filenames. These functional records are not uploaded to the developer or attached to Setapp usage events.</p>
    <p>You can manage saved locations and Authorized Paths in the app and clear the retained Activity list. Recent savings are stored separately from Activity. Do not delete recovery records or temporary recovery files while an operation or unresolved recovery is in progress.</p>
    <h3>CLI and third-party automation</h3>
    <p>The CLI communicates locally with DiskPress. Its output may include paths, filenames, settings, measurements, and per-file results. If you pass that output to an AI agent, script, log service, or another program, that program controls what it stores or transmits. DiskPress does not provide an AI service or send information to one. Using the CLI does not remove the Setapp version's licensing requirements.</p>
    <h3>Application integrity diagnostics</h3>
    <p>If a production copy fails an application integrity check, DiskPress automatically asks your default browser to open a diagnostic help page before stopping. This also applies when the app is serving a CLI command. The URL includes <code>utm_source=diskpress</code> and a numeric <code>utm_content</code> value identifying the failed check. Older app versions used <code>utm_source</code> for the same numeric check identifier. It includes no filenames, local paths, optimization results, or per-user identifier.</p>
    <p>This browser visit is subject to the website analytics and hosting described below. Plausible can count these visits by failure code to help diagnose damaged or modified copies. Normal use and errors optimizing individual files do not trigger this visit. Setapp's app-usage reporting is separate from these diagnostic visits.</p>
    <h3>Services you choose to use</h3>
    <p>Opening website or email links uses the service you selected. A cloud-storage provider, backup service, or automation tool you use may separately store or transmit files and records under its own settings and privacy practices. DiskPress's local processing does not change those services.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="mac-app-store">
    <h2>Mac App Store version</h2>
    <p>The Mac App Store build does not include the Setapp framework or an in-app usage analytics SDK. DiskPress does not report routine launches, menu interactions, or optimization activity in this version. The integrity-diagnostic webpage described above is a separate exception, not routine app telemetry.</p>
    <p>No separate DiskPress account is required. Apple handles the Apple Account, purchase, download, and update services used to obtain this version. Apple may also process optional analytics and crash information according to your system settings. DiskPress does not process your payment-card details.</p>
    <p>Apple's independent services are covered by the <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple privacy policy</a>. Setapp's data collection described in the next section does not apply to the Mac App Store build.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="setapp">
    <h2>Setapp version</h2>
    <p>The Setapp build includes Setapp's framework, which initializes automatically and handles activation. It uses your Setapp account and license rather than a separate DiskPress account. Setapp and its payment providers handle account and billing information. DiskPress does not process your payment-card details.</p>
    <h3>Activation and app-usage reporting</h3>
    <p>Setapp processes licensing, device, usage, and diagnostic information. This can include device identifiers, operating-system and app versions, launch and interaction events, and performance or error information. These data support activation, service operation, troubleshooting, usage measurement, and payments to developers. See <a href="https://setapp.com/privacy-notice">Setapp's privacy notice</a> for its data categories, purposes, retention, sharing, and privacy rights.</p>
    <p>The framework automatically records events such as app launches, foreground and background activity, and termination. DiskPress also reports a user-interaction event when you open its menu bar menu. This event does not include the files you selected, their names, contents, hashes, or optimization results. Setapp documents its event handling in <a href="https://docs.setapp.com/docs/implement-usage-reporting">usage reporting for macOS apps</a>.</p>
    <h3>Local files and offline use</h3>
    <p>Your file processing remains local, but this version is not entirely offline or free of usage reporting. Setapp activation and license checks may require an internet connection. Usage reports can be stored while offline and sent after connectivity returns, as explained in <a href="https://docs.setapp.com/docs/faq#how-do-you-calculate-revenue-shares-if-users-are-offline">Setapp's developer FAQ</a>.</p>
    <p>Setapp's reporting is distinct from the website's Plausible analytics. Blocking website analytics does not disable the Setapp framework. For Setapp account data and privacy requests, use the contacts and controls in <a href="https://setapp.com/privacy-notice">Setapp's privacy notice</a>. Contact the developer below for DiskPress-specific questions.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="website"><h2>Website analytics</h2><p>diskpress.app uses Plausible Analytics through analytics.diskpress.app to understand aggregate website use and improve the site. Measurement includes pages visited, referral and campaign sources, browser and operating-system categories, device types, approximate location derived from the request, and clicks on outbound links.</p><p>Plausible does not use analytics cookies or persistent cross-site identifiers. Its analytics processing derives aggregate information from incoming requests and does not retain raw IP addresses in the analytics dataset. The website does not add advertising trackers or session-replay software.</p><p>Outbound-link events can include the destination URL, such as a Mac App Store or developer-site link. The site does not attach your local files, app Activity, or optimization results to analytics events. For details of Plausible's measurement design, read the <a href="https://plausible.io/data-policy">Plausible data policy</a>.</p><p>The analytics endpoint is distinct from the app. Visiting the website is not necessary for DiskPress to optimize your files.</p></section>
  <section id="hosting"><h2>Hosting and browser preferences</h2><p>The website is delivered through Cloudflare. Serving and securing web requests involves technical information such as IP addresses, request URLs, browser information, routing data, and diagnostic logs. This hosting activity is separate from Plausible's aggregate analytics. Cloudflare explains its processing in its <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">privacy policy</a>.</p><p>If you change the appearance selector, the site saves the value in your browser's local storage under <code>diskpress-appearance</code>. It is used only to remember Light, Dark, or System on that browser. It is not an analytics identifier. Clear the site's browser data to remove it.</p><p>Hosting, analytics infrastructure, and email providers process information needed to provide their services. This policy does not promise a particular country of processing or a fixed provider log-retention period.</p></section>
  <section id="support"><h2>Support messages</h2><p>If you email <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>, the developer receives your email address, message, and anything you attach. This information is used to respond, troubleshoot, and maintain necessary support records. Share only what is needed and remove private paths or sensitive content from screenshots and logs.</p><p>Email support messages are kept only as long as reasonably needed to handle the request, maintain necessary records, or meet legal obligations. You may ask for deletion, subject to those obligations. Information you send for support is not sold or used for targeted advertising.</p><p>You can also use the <a href="/support/">support page</a> to open a GitHub issue. Issues, comments, and attachments are public. GitHub handles that information under its <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">privacy statement</a>. Use email for private matters.</p><p>If you contact Apple or Setapp support instead, that provider handles your message under its own privacy policy.</p></section>
  <section id="choices"><h2>Your choices and privacy rights</h2><p>In either version, you can disable automatic monitoring, remove saved authorizations, and avoid sending optional support information. You can use browser controls or content blockers to limit website analytics. The website remains readable when analytics are blocked. These browser choices do not change Apple's services or Setapp's licensing and usage reporting.</p><p>Depending on the law that applies to you, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, restrict, or object to processing of personal information held by the developer, and to complain to a relevant data-protection authority. Contact the address below to make a request. Plausible's aggregate website analytics generally cannot be connected to a particular visitor, and the developer cannot access app records stored only on your Mac. For information held by Apple or Setapp, follow the rights-request instructions in that provider's policy.</p><p>Where a legal basis is required, necessary hosting and security processing supports operating this website, support processing responds to your request, and records may be retained to meet legal obligations. No claim about cookie-free analytics removes rights that applicable law gives you.</p></section>
  <section id="contact"><h2>Contact and policy updates</h2><p><a href={DEVELOPER_URL}>Ighor July</a> is the developer of DiskPress and the contact for this policy. Send privacy questions or requests to <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.</p><p>This page may be updated when the app, website, or relevant practices change. The date above identifies the current policy. Material changes will be described here. This revision adds separate Mac App Store and Setapp disclosures, including Setapp activation and usage reporting. See the <a href="/terms-of-service/">terms of service</a> for use of the website and application.</p></section>
</DocumentLayout>
